          "text": "7. If A Shell Is Forced"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import shlex",
            "cmd = \"ls \" + shlex.quote(name)",
            "# quoting is last resort; blocklists leak"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Strict allowlist of permitted values first",
            "Then proper quoting, never manual escaping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Remove The Interpreter"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Instead of",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "curl",
              "HTTP client lib"
            ],
            [
              "cp, mv",
              "file APIs"
            ],
            [
              "tar",
              "archive lib"
            ],
            [
              "convert",
              "imaging lib"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Contain The Blast",
          "items": [
            "Run as an unprivileged user",
            "Sandbox or container per job",
            "Read-only mounts, no egress"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Three Distinct Controls",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Control",
            "Asks",
            "Acts at"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Validation",
              "acceptable?",
              "entry"
            ],
            [
              "Parameterisation",
              "code or data?",
              "DB call"
            ],
            [
              "Encoding",
              "safe here?",
              "output"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Validation Is Not The Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Defense in depth, never the primary defense",
            "Valid data can still be a valid attack",
            "O'Brien is a real name and a SQL breaker",
            "Rejecting it breaks users, not attackers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Allowlist Beats Blocklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Approach",
            "Rule",
            "Fails how"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Allowlist",
              "known-good set",
              "too strict"
            ],
            [
              "Blocklist",
              "known-bad list",
              "missed variant"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Constrain by pattern, type, range, and set",
            "Blocklists always miss an encoding or variant"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "ok = re.fullmatch(r\"\\w{3,20}\", u)",
            "if not ok:",
            "    abort(400)  # known-good only"
          ],
          "note": "fullmatch, not search"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Canonicalise First"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Decode to one form, then validate",
            "%3C, double-encoding, %252F",
            "Unicode homoglyphs and overlong UTF-8",
            "Validate once, after normalisation, never before"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from unicodedata import normalize",
            "s = normalize(\"NFKC\", raw)",
            "validate(s)  # never raw"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Where Validation Wins",
          "text": "Type, length, and range checks reject garbage early and shrink the attack surface — they just can't carry the fix alone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Command Injection (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Primary Fix Per Interpreter"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Interpreter",
            "Primary fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SQL",
              "parameterise"
            ],
            [
              "OS shell",
              "array exec"
            ],
            [
              "Browser",
              "context encoding"
            ],
            [
              "Templates",
              "auto-escape on"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Validation vs Encoding",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Right Layer Or Nothing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "SQL escaping does not make data HTML-safe",
            "HTML escaping does not make data shell-safe",
            "There is no universal sanitise() function"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Types Are Free Defense"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "uid = int(request.args[\"id\"])  # ValueError",
            "cur.execute(\"...WHERE id=%s\", (uid,))",
            "# an int cannot carry syntax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Layer Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "validate at entry",
              "parameterise / encode at boundary",
              "least privilege underneath"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Stripping Bad Characters",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "SeLeCt          # case flip",
            "SEL/**/ECT      # inline comment",
            "%2527           # double-encoded quote"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Case, comments, encoding, whitespace all bypass",
            "Stripping quotes changes data and still loses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Hand-Escaping Quotes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Numeric context needs no quotes at all",
            "Backslash edge cases undo the escape",
            "Charset tricks (GBK) rebuild the quote byte"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Sanitise Once, Reuse"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cleaned for HTML, later used in a URL",
            "Wrong context on output re-opens the flaw",
            "Storage should hold raw data, not pre-escaped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Trusting The Browser"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Client validation is UX, not a control",
            "curl sends raw requests with no JS at all",
            "Mobile clients and replayed requests skip it too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Remaining Hole"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = \"SELECT * FROM t ORDER BY \" + col",
            "cur.execute(q, ())  # values safe, name open",
            "# allowlist col before it reaches the string"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. \"The Args Are Internal\""
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "shell=True or exec(string) on trusted values",
            "Internal today, user-influenced next sprint",
            "Second-order path makes it reachable quietly"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. ORM Complacency"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Safe by default, unsafe on every raw escape hatch",
            "Grep for raw(), text(), execute(), interpolation",
            "One f-string in a repository undoes the layer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Turning Escaping Off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "dangerouslySetInnerHTML or |safe for convenience",
            "No sanitiser behind the bypass",
            "Every hatch needs DOMPurify or a review note"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. WAF As The Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bypassable by encoding and fragmentation",
            "A stopgap that buys time, not safety",
            "Never close the ticket on a WAF rule"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Loud Errors In Prod"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stack traces hand over schema and versions",
            "Log detail server-side, show a generic message",
            "Verbose errors turn blind SQLi into easy mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One Mental Model",
          "text": "Every injection is code/data confusion at an interpreter boundary. Keep the two separate and the class disappears."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. SQL",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always parameterise; never concatenate",
            "Allowlist identifiers and ORDER BY choices",
            "Least-privilege DB account, no DDL",
            "Audit ORM raw escape hatches"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. XSS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Context-aware output encoding, every sink",
            "Prefer textContent over innerHTML",
            "Sanitise required HTML with DOMPurify",
            "CSP and HttpOnly as depth, not as the fix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Command"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Avoid the shell; pass args as an array",
            "Allowlist plus shlex.quote when forced",
            "Sandbox and least privilege underneath",
            "Native library beats shelling out"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Validation's Place"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Supporting layer, never the sole defense",
            "Allowlist, and canonicalise before checking"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Encode and parameterise at the boundary",
            "Per context, per sink, at output time",
            "Not once at input, not globally"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
